  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize capturing Heart cards and the Seven of Hearts above all else. Try to leave your opponent with no combinations that sum to 10 (the maximum face card value).\n\nDenial: If you see the table has a 3, a 4, and an Ace (Sum = 8), and you don't have an 8, avoid playing a card that would make the total sum to a Jack, Queen, or King.\n\nCounting 7s: The Sevens are the most powerful cards for building combinations. If you know three 7s are gone, you can safely play high cards without fearing a Hurrikan.",
    Player: "Prioritize capturing Heart cards and the Seven of Hearts above all else. Try to leave your opponent with no combinations that sum to 10 (the maximum face card value).\n\nDenial: If you see the table has a 3, a 4, and an Ace (Sum = 8), and you don't have an 8, avoid playing a card that would make the total sum to a Jack, Queen, or King.\n\nCounting 7s: The Sevens are the most powerful cards for building combinations. If you know three 7s are gone, you can safely play high cards without fearing a Hurrikan.",
