    basic: 'Prioritize capturing Heart cards and the Seven of Hearts above all else. Try to leave your opponent with no combinations that sum to 10 (the maximum face card value).',
    intermediate: "Denial: If you see the table has a 3, a 4, and an Ace (Sum = 8), and you don't have an 8, avoid playing a card that would make the total sum to a Jack, Queen, or King.",
    advanced: 'Counting 7s: The Sevens are the most powerful cards for building combinations. If you know three 7s are gone, you can safely play high cards without fearing a Hurrikan.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Save your '10' (King) for when the board has many low cards that sum to 10.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Never leave a single card on the table if you can help it, as it's an easy setup for an opponent's Hurrikan.",
